-- Review repair pinned by this corpus (2026-08-16): a module-level open fact
-- (a section GIVEN; a module-level ASSUME until 2026-09-06, which lowers the
-- same way) referenced ONLY from inside an inlined parameterized DECIDE must
-- still survive as a question block. Before the repair, the emitted code resolved
-- `base rate` to a variable while no block defined it: `l4 docassemble`
-- exited 0 and the interview died at runtime with DAErrorMissingVariable —
-- no compile-time diagnostic anywhere.
--
-- No #EVAL oracle here: the fact is never supplied, so this module type-checks
-- but does not evaluate. The round-trip fixtures in roundtrip_check.py carry
-- hand-computed expectations instead (amount 60 + base rate 50 = 110 > 100).

§ `Threshold`
    GIVEN `base rate` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `adjusted` x IS x PLUS `base rate`

@export Whether the amount exceeds the adjusted threshold
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `over threshold` amount IF `adjusted` amount GREATER THAN 100
